      "mergedPostDetails": "You can configure a world to not support portals, you can disable items by default, but for both it's world-wide. I think you should be able to define zones that are exceptions to those.\n\nExample: Murder 4\n\nI don't want people placing portals in the Mansion, but at spawn is OK.\n\nWhat do I do?\n\nThis proposal lets you disable portals world-wide and then add an exception to the spawn area.\n\nExample 2: Wide hallway\n\nI can't get to the other side of the map without going through this hallway but some jerk won't stop putting a trampoline in the middle, making it terrible to use the map.\n\nWhat do I do?\n\nPlace a VRC Feature Restriction Zone that disables placed props that affect gameplay.\n\nThis expands upon https://feedback.vrchat.com/feature-requests/p/feature-request-explicit-no-stickers-emoji-prints-portals-etc-control-zones-in-w",
      "mergedPostTitle": "VRC Feature Restriction Zones",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "608cbb519310c440b0d39adc",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": {
        "like": 0
      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The first part is a duplicate of a feature announced to be in progress: https://feedback.vrchat.com/udon/p/world-request-designating-portal-drop-zones",
      "viewerReactions": null,
