      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Part of @{61665e3e7448d57ed9eb49da|full_name} suggest is pretty good though. If the whole world is set to disallow portals everywhere, and the world creator then has to place dedicated \"portal allowed zones\" in the world. This would then be simple for VRChat to locally determine the closet zone and point the user towards it with an arrow. (Like I suggest in a previous comment here.)\n\nFeature could automatically enable if one of these zones are placed somewhere in the world, or give a warning on the SDK build screen if portals are disabled world-wide with no \"portal allowed zones\" placed anywhere.\n\nWorld creators could also use these zones to gently notch people through teleporters, if a size zero zone is placed on it to make the arrow point the user to it. (Or use it as obscure puzzle hints, I guess.)",
